/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-formats","content":"What file formats can I upload, and how big?"},"3099":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-28","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-duration","content":"Why does it ask for the duration on an imported video?"},"3100":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-29","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-storage","content":"Do imported videos use my storage?"},"3101":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-30","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-allowance","content":"How much storage do I have?"},"3102":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-31","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-past-recording","content":"Can I use a recording of a webinar I already ran?"},"3103":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-32","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-change-video","content":"Can I change the video on a webinar later?"},"3104":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-33","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-during-setup","content":"Can I add a video without leaving webinar setup?"},"3105":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-34","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#faq-youtube-private","content":"Is a YouTube-hosted webinar video private?"},"3106":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-35","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#related","content":"Related"},"3107":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-36","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","content":"Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording, so before you can run one you need a video in your library. EasyWebinar gives you two ways to get it there. **Local import** uploads the file and EasyWebinar hosts it for you, so you don't need a separate video host. **Import from URL** plays a video that already lives on **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or at a direct **MP4** link. The route you pick decides whether the video uses your storage and whether you need to tell EasyWebinar how long it runs."},"3108":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-37","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|         | Host on EasyWebinar | Import from a URL   |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ------------------- |\n| **How** | **Local import**    | **Import from URL** |","table":"table-0"},"3109":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-38","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|                           | Host on EasyWebinar              | Import from a URL                                      |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Where the video lives** | Stored and served by EasyWebinar | Stays on YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or the MP4 link's host |","table":"table-0"},"3110":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-39","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|                     | Host on EasyWebinar     | Import from a URL         |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **Format and size** | **MP4**, up to **4 GB** | Not stored on EasyWebinar |","table":"table-0"},"3111":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-40","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|             | Host on EasyWebinar                     | Import from a URL |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| **Storage** | Counts towards your account's allowance | None used         |","table":"table-0"},"3112":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-41","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|              | Host on EasyWebinar              | Import from a URL                          |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Duration** | Read automatically from the file | You enter it in hours, minutes and seconds |","table":"table-0"},"3113":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-42","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|                   | Host on EasyWebinar | Import from a URL       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| **Library badge** | **EasyWebinar**     | The platform's own logo |","table":"table-0"},"3114":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-43","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"|               | Host on EasyWebinar                                             | Import from a URL                        |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **Good when** | The video isn't published anywhere, or you want it kept private | It's already on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia |","table":"table-0"},"3115":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-44","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#at-a-glance","content":"Both routes start from **Library → Add Media**, or from **Add Video** while you set up a simulive or evergreen webinar. Either way the video lands in your library and can be reused on other webinars."},"3116":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-45","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#what-it-is","content":"Video hosting answers a practical question: where does the file your automated webinar plays actually live?"},"3117":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-46","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#what-it-is","content":"With **Local import**, the answer is EasyWebinar. You upload the file, EasyWebinar stores and serves it in the same way a dedicated video host would, and nothing else is needed to play it in a webinar. The upload uses part of your storage allowance, shown at the top of the Library."},"3118":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-47","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#what-it-is","content":"With **Import from URL**, the answer is somewhere else. You give EasyWebinar the platform, a link and the video's length, and the webinar plays the video from that platform. Nothing is stored on EasyWebinar, so no storage is used, but the webinar now depends on the video staying where it is."},"3119":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-48","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#what-it-is","content":"Live webinars don't need either. You supply their content by presenting, and recordings of those live sessions land in your library automatically when recording is on."},"3120":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-49","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#what-its-for","content":"Hosting is what lets a recorded webinar run. Simulive webinars play the video at times you set, and evergreen webinars play it whenever a registrant's session comes round. Neither works until the video is in the library."},"3121":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-50","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#how-it-helps","content":"**No separate video host to set up.** **Local import** means a recorded webinar can run with nothing outside EasyWebinar."},"3122":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-51","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#how-it-helps","content":"**Private videos stay private.** A webinar recording you don't want public can be hosted on EasyWebinar instead of a public platform."},"3123":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-52","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#how-it-helps","content":"**Existing videos work as they are.** If the video is already on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia, you import the link and use no storage."},"3124":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-53","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#how-it-helps","content":"**One library, many webinars.** A video added once can be reused across webinars."},"3125":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-54","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#how-it-helps","content":"**Easy to swap.** The **Webinar Video** panel changes a webinar's video without touching its schedule, pages or registrations."},"3126":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-55","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#without-it","content":"Without built-in hosting, every recorded webinar would depend on another platform: an account to manage, privacy settings to get right, and a video that anyone with access to that channel could remove. A YouTube video is still a YouTube video, discoverable unless you've unlisted it. Hosting on EasyWebinar keeps the recording and the webinar in one place."},"3127":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-56","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#why-buyers-care","content":"Teams moving to automated webinars want to know whether they need a video host as well as a webinar platform. In EasyWebinar they don't: uploads are hosted directly, and importing from YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia is an option rather than a requirement. Buyers also check file formats and size limits before recording, and how storage is counted when a library grows."},"3128":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-57","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"Click **Library** in the sidebar, then **Add Media**."},"3129":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-58","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"Choose **Local import**."},"3130":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-59","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"Give the video a title. This is the name you'll see in your library."},"3131":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-60","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"Drop your file onto the box, or click it to browse."},"3132":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-61","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"Click **Upload**."},"3133":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-62","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"|     | Control          | What it does                                                        |\n| --- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1   | **Local import** | Uploads from your computer. EasyWebinar stores and serves the video |","table":"table-1"},"3134":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting-63","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/media/video-hosting#host-on-easywebinar","content":"| 