],[1315,"**Keep deadlines consistent.** Match the offer countdown, the replay deadline and what your follow-up emails say."],[1169,"**Keep host answers accurate.** An `Admin` reply is read as your answer, so it should be one you'd give live."],[2862,"**Keep live recording on** if you want your sessions to land here. Recording is on by default in the live room, where the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled**."],[1574,"**Keep options short and distinct**, so each one can be read at a glance."],[3408,"**Keep them short.** A reminder needs the time and the link."],[2861,"**Know what uses storage.** Only files uploaded to EasyWebinar count towards your storage. Videos imported from a URL use none."],[542,"**Know which campaign worked.** Turn on **UTM Params** so each registration records the ad, email or post that brought it in."],[1978,"**Know which type you want the copy to be.** You choose it in the dialog, and it is fixed on the new webinar once created."],[138,"**Know your audience and offer.** The prompt drives everything. Have a specific audience, three or four teaching points, a length, a tone, and what you'll sell at the end ready before you start."],[2386,"**Know your audience's hours.** Recurring sessions run in the webinar's timezone, so pick times that work for the people you expect."],[2863,"**Know your upload limit.** Upload video as **MP4**, up to **4 GB** per file. See video and storage limits."],[1121,"**Know your video.** For a manual script, you'll time messages against the recording, so have it to hand."],[4003,"**Known contacts skip the form.** The **One-Click Registration Link** registers someone you already have details for without asking them to type them again."],[754,"**Lead score is calculated from engagement.** It's a guide for sorting, not a replacement for the underlying columns."],[739,"**Lead score** is calculated from engagement: attendance, watch time and interaction. It rates how engaged someone was, for example **Hot**, so you can sort a long list and start with the most engaged people. It's a quick way to prioritise. For the detail, read it alongside **Status**, **Watch percentage**, **Polls** and **Offer clicked** on the same row."],[1715,"**Leave time at the end** to clear what's left in Active before you close."],[1160,"**Let it breathe.** Real chat comes in bursts with quiet stretches, not one message every thirty seconds."],[1157,"**Line messages up with the video.** A question about a slide should land while that slide is on screen."],[2128,"**Live + Replay bundle**, to sell access to the webinar and its recording together"],[623,"**Live and automated in one place.** EasyWebinar can run the same course webinar live, simulive or evergreen. eWebinar runs recorded sessions, so it covers the automated half of a launch. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[899,"**Live and replay in one count.** EasyWebinar's **Total Attended** shows unique people, split into **Live only**, **Replay only** and **Both**. WebinarJam shows live and replay data separately, and Zoom reports recording views on Webinars Plus. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar and EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[4366,"**Live Attended** counts people who joined the live session. **Total Attended** adds replay viewers, so it's the larger number."],[848,"**Live Attended** covers the broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts each person once whether they watched live, on replay or both, which is why it's the number to use when you ask how many people the webinar reached."],[909,"**Live Attended** is the live broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts unique people who watched live or on replay."],[374,"**Live attendees** counts people joining live sessions in the current period."],[2897,"**Live sessions become reusable content.** A recording can be picked as the video for a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[2127,"**Live webinar price**, in US dollars"],[2479,"**Live webinars built in.** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars from one account. eWebinar's public docs show no live video broadcast, and StealthSeminar streams live video in from YouTube Live or Twitch. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar and EasyWebinar vs Stealth Seminar."],[3186,"**Live webinars don't need a video.** Simulive and evergreen webinars are the types that play one."],[1607,"**Live webinars need manual launches.** On a live webinar, each poll is launched from the **Polls** panel."],[1332,"**Live-room timers are different.** Once you go live, the room header shows **LIVE** with a timer of how long you have been broadcasting. That timer counts up and is separate from offer countdowns."],[2250,"**Local import** uploads a file from your computer, and EasyWebinar stores and serves it. No YouTube or Vimeo account is involved."],[1034,"**Local time applies to just-in-time sessions only.** Other sessions on the same webinar use the webinar's timezone."],[3640,"**Make it mandatory if you need to.** You can require the box to be ticked before someone can register."],[554,"**Manual Simulation** plays a chat you script yourself in a CSV, timed against your video."],[1110,"**Manual Simulation**: you write every line yourself, with a timestamp, a name and a role."],[3305,"**Merge tags come pre-filled on AI-built emails.** If you rewrite an AI draft, keep the tags that carry the date, time and join link."],[3416,"**Missed** counts people who registered and never showed up. Add a **Webinar Follow-up** with its audience set to no-shows and include the replay link. In **People**, filter by **Behavior** for no-shows to see exactly who they are, then **Export** the list if you need it elsewhere."],[852,"**Missed** is the group most worth contacting after a session. Send them the replay."],[2601,"**Mistakes stay private.** Audio checks and false starts happen before the broadcast, not at the top of the recording."],[1159,"**Mix the roles.** Attendee questions answered by `Admin` replies read as a conversation. Attendee messages alone read 