t take questions at all."],[897,"**Offer results.** EasyWebinar's **Offers Performance** shows views, clicks and purchases for each offer. Demio's Featured Action shows clicks and the share of attendees who clicked, and its docs describe no purchase tracking. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1905,"**Offer revenue and registration revenue are reported separately**, under **Paid Offer** and **Paid Webinar**."],[3050,"**Offers and polls carry over only with Webinar Replica.** A **Custom Build** page has its own layout and CTAs."],[134,"**Offers match your pitch.** You choose how hard to sell, and the offers come back complete with a headline, button and link."],[879,"**Offers Performance** reports on the offers you build on the **CTAs** tab. Comparing sessions is the clearest way to see whether a change, such as adding a countdown timer, helped."],[4319,"**On a free webinar** the panel reads \"This webinar is free — attendees register without payment,\" with a **Convert to paid** button."],[4320,"**On a paid webinar** the panel shows your pricing title and price, and the pencil edits them. A **Payment Gateway** panel shows the connected Stripe account, and **Manage** opens your payment settings."],[1255,"**On a registration page**, it tells visitors how soon the session begins, which turns \"sometime\" into \"in two days\"."],[1254,"**On an offer**, it tells attendees how long they have to act on what you are selling: a course enrolment, a coaching call, a bonus, a programme."],[3487,"**On Demand** is an evergreen schedule setting that lets a registrant start watching your webinar straight away, with no session to wait for. EasyWebinar also calls it **instant replay**: registrants click a button, labelled *Watch instant replay* unless you change it, and the recording starts. It is a different thing from the replay page on the **Replay** tab, which shows the recording of a session that has already happened."],[1019,"**On Demand** lets registrants watch immediately, with no 