ube or Vimeo?"],[1244,"Does EasyWebinar write the offer for me?"],[1238,"Does every offer need a countdown?"],[676,"Does Export include only the filtered people?"],[110,"Does it work for simulive and evergreen webinars?"],[1094,"Does it work with a third-party chat tool?"],[2194,"Does my video need to be on YouTube or Vimeo first?"],[1666,"Does Q&A work on simulive webinars?"],[811,"Does replay viewing count as attendance?"],[2368,"Does the webinar ever stop running?"],[1145,"Drag the file onto the upload area, or use **Choose File**."],[3131,"Drop your file onto the box, or click it to browse."],[3389,"Each entry shows its **trigger**, the audience it goes **to**, and its **subject**, so the group reads as a timeline of what registrants will receive."],[31,"Each member needs their own email address."],[1813,"Each offer has:"],[3848,"Each page has a working default, so you don't have to design any of them. If you only have time for two, make them the registration page and the replay page."],[702,"Each row is one person on one webinar, with columns including:"],[4316,"Each row shows the date, time, timezone and registration count for that sitting. A one-time webinar has a single upcoming session. A daily or weekly webinar fills the list from its recurrence, and a daily evergreen schedule generates a long run of upcoming sessions without you adding any."],[4175,"Each transaction shows one of these statuses: **Pending**, **Processing**, **Success**, **Failed**, **Canceled**, **Refunded** or **Partially Refunded**. An attendee is registered once their payment succeeds."],[2022,"Each type delivers content differently, but pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics are shared across all three. That's why a clone can carry those assets into a different type."],[50,"Each webinar's **Team & Moderators** panel shows everyone who can run that webinar. **Add presenter** adds someone who appears on camera and presents. **Invite** sends an invitation to join the webinar team. The Overview page explains how presenters differ from team members."],[2570,"EasyCast"],[2695,"EasyCast"],[2642,"EasyCast destinations are switched on in the green room, before you go live. Once the broadcast starts, a platform icon for each destination appears in the top bar. Connections are made once, under **Integrations → EasyCast** in the sidebar, and work across every webinar."],[2755,"EasyCast is set up per account, so a destination connected once is available on every webinar. It covers **YouTube**, **LinkedIn**, **LinkedIn Organisation** and **Custom RTMP**."],[2788,"EasyCast multistreaming sends the live session to YouTube, LinkedIn, LinkedIn Organisation pages and custom RTMP destinations, connected once under **Integrations → EasyCast** and switched on per session in the room. Facebook isn't offered as a destination; its RTMP details may work under **Custom RTMP**."],[272,"EasyCRM"],[364,"EasyCRM sending allowance"],[1266,"EasyWebinar builds the countdown into the offer card itself. On the **CTAs** tab, the coach opens the programme offer and switches on **Countdown timer**. The bonus goes in the **Headline**, so the card says what ends. Because the timer is part of the offer, it appears in every session that shows that offer. With the replay page set to **Webinar Replica**, the offer carries over to the replay too."],[3149,"EasyWebinar can't read the length of a video hosted elsewhere, and it uses the duration to schedule sessions and work out when the webinar ends. A wrong figure cuts the video short or leaves attendees waiting on a finished one."],[635,"EasyWebinar connects with Kit (ConvertKit), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, Drip, AWeber, Keap, Ontraport, GetResponse, Constant Contact and GoHighLevel, and tags people by what they did in the webinar."],[1540,"EasyWebinar groups the things you put in front of an audience under **CTAs**, and there are two kinds. An offer sells something. A poll asks something. Both appear in the room only when you decide to show them."],[524,"EasyWebinar handles both halves of that launch. The creator runs a **Live** webinar with recording on, then clones it as an **Evergreen** webinar. The copy plays the recording at a time each registrant picks. The live original is untouched, and the evergreen copy takes over for everyone who joins the list later."],[2269,"EasyWebinar has three webinar types, and they differ only in how the content is delivered. Pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics are the same across all three."],[1247,"EasyWebinar has two countdowns. An **offer countdown** sits on an offer card in the webinar room and shows how long that offer stays open. A **registration-page countdown** shows how long is left until the session starts. Both are built in, and neither needs a separate timer tool or embedded widget."],[3137,"EasyWebinar hosts the file from then on. Upload **MP4** files up to **4 GB**, and EasyWebinar reads the video's length automatically."],[3188,"EasyWebinar hosts them. **Local import** uploads your file and serves it, with no other video host involved. Importing from a URL is an option, not a requirement."],[240,"EasyWebinar is a webinar platform for running live and recorded webinars that collect leads and sell. You build a webinar with a registration page, emails, polls and offers, run it live or from a recording, and follow up through analytics, integrations and the built-in EasyCRM."],[4140,"EasyWebinar makes checkout the final step of signing up. The consultant chooses **Paid** on the pricing step while creating the webinar, and **Register Now** on the registration page then opens a Stripe checkout. EasyWebinar registers a founder only once their payment goes through. It then sends them to the thank-you page, which shows their personal join link."],[232,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[1316,"EasyWebinar puts a countdown on the offer and another on the registration page itself. The offer countdown works the same way on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[3191,"EasyWebinar reads the length of an uploaded file automatically, but not of one hosted elsewhere. It needs the duration to schedule sessions correctly."],[2254,"EasyWebinar reads the length of an uploaded file itself, but not of a linked one. It uses the duration to schedule sessions and to know when the webinar ends, so a wrong figure can cut the video short or leave attendees waiting after it has finished."],[614,"EasyWebinar runs the webinar that sells your course, live or automated, in one product. The enrolment offer appears inside the room, and it can carry a countdown. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[628,"EasyWebinar sells your course; it doesn't host or deliver it. Lessons, student logins and course progress stay on your course platform. The offer button and replay redirect send buyers there."],[4189,"EasyWebinar takes payment as part of sign-up: **Register Now** opens a Stripe checkout, and the person is registered once they've paid. It can also sell the replay at its own price, and it lists every payment against the webinar. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[2452,"EasyWebinar turns that recording into one evergreen webinar with a single schedule. The team keeps its Tuesday slot as a **Weekly** **Recurring Schedule** and switches on **Just-in-time Registration** beside it. The registration page offers both as choices, so the Wednesday prospect can take a session that begins minutes later instead of next week."],[837,"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab does that count for each webinar. Its **Overview** view runs from **Visitors** and **Registered** through **Live Attended** and **Replay Watched**. Further down, **Offers Performance** reports each offer's views and clicks. For this team, that shows whether the extra registrants stopped before the session, during it, or at the demo button."],[887,"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab follows one webinar from page visits to offer sales and revenue. It reports each offer's purchases next to its views and clicks, and counts live and replay viewers without double counting. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[3335,"Edit a reminder"],[3802,"Edit blocks"],[4187,"Educators in fields such as real estate, finance or wellness run paid seminars. Paid registration keeps the attendee list limited to people who paid, and the transaction list gives a record of every purchase."],[911,"Either the webinar hasn't run yet, or your date range doesn't cover the period when it did."],[2253,"Either way, the video is saved to your library and can be reused on other webinars. For the full upload and import walkthrough, see Video hosting."],[94,"Emails"],[3468,"Emails"],[4084,"Emails"],[945,"Emails and reminders"],[2180,"Emails and reminders"],[2349,"Emails and reminders"],[1365,"Embed a third-party chat tool"],[3811,"Embedding the form on your own site"],[1716,"Ending the session disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin, so finish the questions you want to answer before you click **End Session**."],[3281,"Enter a **Reply-to email**."],[3280,"Enter a **Sender name**."],[3142,"Enter the **Video duration** in hours, minutes and seconds."],[2392,"Enter the **Webinar Name** your registrants will see."],[2671,"Enter the EasyWebinar webinar room, prepare in the green room, go live, present with chat, polls, offers and Q&A, then end the session and find your recording."],[1581,"Enter the room from the webinar's **Overview** with **Enter Room**."],[451,"Enter the room well before your start time. The green room broadcasts nothing, so you can pass the device check, finish your checks and test **Share** before anyone is watching. Close other video-call tools before you click **Enter Room**, so nothing else is holding the camera. For the kit itself, see the webinar equipment guide and this host preparation guide."],[37,"Enter their **Name** and **Email**, and optionally a **Photo**."],[4242,"Entering a running session on a recorded webinar"],[2508,"Evergreen"],[3342,"Evergreen and just-in-time sessions"],[2468,"Evergreen features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[2694,"Evergreen from a live session"],[4091,"Evergreen paid trainings"],[1075,"Evergreen schedules"],[2442,"Evergreen suits a webinar that belongs to a funnel and should work whether or not you're free. Typical examples are a product demo, customer onboarding or a year-round offer. People reach it at all hours, so it has to be ready whenever they do."],[2456,"Evergreen webinars can use **Easywebinar Chat**, embed an external chat tool with **Third party**, or turn chat off with **No Chat** while keeping the **EW Contact Box** for questions sent by email."],[1021,"Evergreen webinars have a **Live** tab in the Sessions panel, alongside **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**, showing sessions currently on air. See The Overview tab."],[1364,"Evergreen: simulate the room"],[3986,"Every EasyWebinar webinar generates seven links, and the **Share** button on the webinar's header shows them all in one dialog. One is the public registration link you promote; others let a known contact register in one click, let attendees join, let a co-presenter or moderator into the room, and send people to the replay. The dialog also holds the **Registration Widget** embed code, a **Share on social media** section, and a **Shorten URL's** toggle for shorter versions of every link."],[813,"Every EasyWebinar webinar has an **Analytics** tab that shows how many people reached each stage of that webinar and where the rest dropped away. It has three views: **Overview** for the funnel, engagement and offer numbers, **People** for the individuals behind those numbers, and **Revenue** for what the webinar earned. A date range at the top limits everything on the page to the period you choose."],[4274,"Every EasyWebinar webinar opens on its **Overview** tab. From this one screen you can see how the webinar is doing, check and change when it runs, act on a single session, switch between free and paid registration, add the people who present or moderate, and get to the share links and the room. This page walks through each panel in the order you'll usually need it. When you're done, you'll know where every webinar-level control on the Overview lives and what each number means."],[358,"Every limit, allowance and default setting in EasyWebinar in one place, with its unit and where it applies."],[256,"Every page shows who it applies to, its status and the date it was last checked against the product. Each heading has a permanent link you can copy and share."],[1545,"Every poll on a webinar sits in one list on the CTAs tab. Each one can be switched on or off from that list without being deleted, so a poll can wait in reserve until the point in the session where it fits."],[4028,"Every public link includes your subdomain, ending in `.easywebinar.live`, including the links in your emails. The **C-Name** add-on lets links use your own domain instead. Changing your subdomain changes your existing links, so anything already shared will break; set it before you promote."],[836,"Every stage up to the demo button happens on the webinar platform: the page visit, the sign-up, the session, the recording and the click. A platform that runs all of those can count every stage for the same webinar, so nobody has to merge lists by hand."],[2288,"Every video you add, and every recording of a past webinar, lands in the **Library**. Recordings appear there automatically when **Auto Recording** is on in the live room. See The Library."],[3171,"Every video you add, by either route, appears on the Library's **Videos** tab with a badge in its corner: **EasyWebinar** for a hosted file, or the platform's logo for an imported link. Recordings of live sessions appear on the **Recordings** tab."],[3728,"Every webinar has a registration page hosted by EasyWebinar, and a **Registration Page Link** that sends people to it. The Registration Widget is the other route: instead of sending visitors to EasyWebinar, you bring the form to them, on a page you already control."],[3846,"Every webinar has five pages that its audience moves through: **Registration Page**, **Thank you Page**, **Waiting Area**, **Webinar Page** and **Replay Page**. All five open in the same builder, and all five already know when your webinar runs."],[3385,"Every webinar result that matters to the business, offer clicks, purchases, booked calls, depends on people actually watching. A platform's reminders decide how many registrants make it into that group. Buyers look for reminders that need no manual scheduling, work on automated webinars, and can be added and timed freely."],[3253,"Every webinar's **Notifications** tab has three channels: **Emails**, **SMS** and **Whatsapp**. SMS and WhatsApp are in Beta. The **Emails** channel groups everything your webinar sends into five kinds of email:"],[410,"Everything EasyCRM sends draws on this monthly allowance, and its **Wallet** screen shows what's left. The allowance resets on your **signup date**, not the first of the month. Broadcasts and workflows draw on the same allowance, and each channel is counted separately."],[2760,"Everything you use while presenting sits on the right-hand rail:"],[3966,"Expired links"],[1563,"Fill in the **Response Options**. Click **Add another option** for each extra answer, and click the bin beside any option to remove it."],[1271,"Fill in the rest of the offer: **Offer Style** (**Text Offer** or **Image Offer**), **Offer Price** (or switch on **Free**), the **Headline** and **Sub Headline**, and the **Button** text and URL."],[1054,"Fill the chat on a simulive or evergreen webinar with a conversation generated by AI from a cast of simulated attendees, or scripted by you in a timed CSV."],[762,"Filter **Behavior** for high watch time and offer clicks. Those are people who were interested and haven't bought yet."],[737,"Filter **People** by **Source & UTM** to see which campaign each registrant came from."],[755,"Filter by **Behavior** for no-shows, add a **Webinar** filter for a single event, then click **Export**."],[757,"Filter by **Source & UTM**. You need **UTM Params** turned on in your registration form first."],[3859,"Filter by category: **All Templates**, **Agency**, **Coach**, **Education**, **Health & Wellness**, **Lead Magnet** or **Marketing**. **My Templates** holds templates you've saved yourself."],[2132,"Filter by category: **All Templates**, **Agency**, **Coach**, **Education**, **Health & Wellness**, **Lead Magnet**, **Marketing**, or **My Templates** for ones you have saved."],[732,"Filter first, then export. Exporting everything and cutting it down in a spreadsheet repeats work the filters already do, and **Export** respects whatever filters are applied."],[3274,"Find the **Registration Confirmation** group at the top of the list."],[1982,"Find the webinar to copy. The type filters (**All**, **Live**, **Simulive**, **Evergreen**, **Archived**) and search help with a long list."],[236,"Find what you need by role"],[1763,"Find your offers"],[1499,"Find your polls"],[3334,"Find your reminders"],[300,"Find your tool under **Available integrations** and click **Connect**."],[2818,"Find, add and manage the videos, webinar recordings, images and documents your webinars use, see which files count towards your storage, and put a library video to work in a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[180,"First choose how you want to position the offer:"],[428,"Fix it"],[482,"Follow up"],[768,"Follow up after a course webinar: how a course creator acts on the people who clicked but didn't enrol."],[1650,"Follow-up"],[1226,"Follow-up and CRM tags"],[662,"Follow-up emails"],[788,"Follow-up emails"],[1775,"Follow-up emails"],[2952,"Follow-up emails"],[584,"Follow-up emails send after the webinar to the audience you choose: everyone who registered, only those who attended, or only the no-shows. No-shows are usually the biggest group, and the replay link is what they want."],[3344,"Follow-ups for people the reminders didn't reach"],[136,"For a coach, course creator or small team, the hours before a first webinar are the main barrier to running one. Buyers want to know how much of the setup a platform can draft for them, whether the output is editable, and what it costs to generate. Create with AI answers all three: five deliverables, all editable, with a visible credit cost per step."],[4019,"For a moderator, to handle chat and questions. Like the co-presenter link, it works without an account. It's also a handy way to check your own webinar from the inside: on a recorded webinar with an embedded third-party chat, joining with the **Moderator Join Link** lets you look at the side panel."],[1310,"For a paid workshop, the registration-page countdown shows how long is left to register before the session starts. Inside the workshop, a countdown on an offer can mark a follow-on programme available to attendees only."],[4018,"For a presenter, so they can join the room. They don't need an EasyWebinar account to use it. When a co-host or moderator joins a live session, they land backstage, not on stage, and your audience doesn't see or hear them until you move them to the stage."],[826,"For a quick read without opening the tab, the webinar's **Overview** tab shows four live stats (**Registrants**, **Live Attended**, **Total Attended** and **Revenue**) that update as the webinar runs. See The Overview tab."],[1172,"For an automated webinar that should still feel busy, pair **Everyone** chat and Chat Simulation with **Private Q&A**, so real questions reach your team in a queue."],[2884,"For an imported video you also enter its length, because EasyWebinar needs the duration to schedule sessions. See Video hosting for both routes step by step."],[3002,"For anyone running webinars to generate leads or sales, the replay decides how much value a single session produces. Buyers check whether replays can expire, whether offers carry over, whether the replay can redirect to a sales page, and whether replay viewing is reported separately from live attendance. EasyWebinar covers each of these on one tab per webinar."],[1827,"For course creators, coaches, consultants and product teams, the offer is where a webinar earns its keep. Buyers check how quickly an offer can be built, whether it can carry a deadline, whether it survives onto the replay, and whether clicks and revenue are reported against each webinar."],[153,"For example: a 45-minute live masterclass for experienced freelance designers who want recurring revenue without hiring, covering why hourly billing caps growth, how to turn a repeatable service into a fixed-scope offer, and how to price it. Warm and practical, no hype. End with an offer for a six-week group programme with templates and weekly calls, plus its price."],[2492,"For just-in-time sessions, yes. Daily and weekly sessions run in the webinar's timezone."],[880,"For paid webinars, the **Revenue** view is where every registration payment and its status appear. See Paid webinars."],[4015,"For people watching the recording afterwards. It's the same link as the **Replay Page Link** on the webinar's **Replay** tab, where you also turn the replay page on with **Enable replay page**."],[3520,"For pricing, video selection and templates, see Create an evergreen webinar."],[4014,"For registered attendees, to enter the live session. Registrants also receive a join link in the **Registration Confirmation** email, which is sent the moment someone registers. That's why it's the one email you shouldn't turn off."],[3620,"For teams that run webinars to generate leads or sell, the registration form is where first-party data starts. Buyers check whether they can add their own questions, collect phone numbers for reminders, ask for consent on the form itself, and attribute each registrant to a campaign without a separate tool."],[988,"For teams who measure an evergreen webinar by how many registrants actually watch, the time between registering and the session starting matters. Just-in-time shrinks it to minutes, using the same recording and the same funnel."],[2441,"For the scheduled-broadcast version, see Create a simulive webinar."],[3631,"Form changes reach visitors only once the page is published. **Save** keeps a draft; **Publish** makes it public."],[1191,"Four columns, `HH:MM:SS,Name,Role,Message`, saved as UTF-8 CSV. **Download sample CSV** gives you the exact layout."],[2512,"From registration to follow-up"],[3694,"From the Content tab"],[3695,"From the Share dialog"],[853,"Further down the **Overview**:"],[176,"gathering background"],[174,"gauging interest in your offer"],[1869,"Generated offers appear on the CTAs tab and are edited like any other. Read the copy before you publish, particularly anything about price and what's included."],[201,"Generated pages open in the same drag-and-drop builder as any other, on the webinar's **Content** tab. Change templates, edit blocks, add **UTM Params** to the form, then publish. See Registration page builder."],[203,"Generated polls and offers appear on the **CTAs** tab, already written and editable like any other. See Polls and Offers."],[1596,"Generated polls land on the CTAs tab and are edited like any poll you wrote yourself. Read them against your script before the webinar."],[3693,"Get the embed code"],[177,"getting feedback on delivery"],[3379,"Getting people to register is the easy part; getting them to turn up is what notifications are for. Reminders carry the date, the time and the way in back to the registrant at the points where they would otherwise drift away: the day before, when they can still plan around it, and the minutes before, when they need a prompt to click."],[480,"Getting people to turn up"],[45,"Give **Admin** to people who need to change billing, team or account settings. **User** suits presenters, moderators and anyone who works on webinars without touching the account."],[2,"Give colleagues their own EasyWebinar login, choose Admin or User, and understand how team members differ from presenters and moderators."],[1443,"Give the box a **Box title**. Attendees see it above the widget, so a plain label such as \"Live Chat\" or \"Ask the team\" works better than the tool's name."],[1840,"Give the offer an internal **Title**, then write the **Headline** and **Sub Headline**."],[3141,"Give the video a title and paste the **Video URL**."],[3130,"Give the video a title. This is the name you'll see in your library."],[3079,"Host a video on EasyWebinar"],[3071,"Host a webinar video on EasyWebinar with Local import, or play one from YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link, with the formats, size limit, storage rules and duration setting for each route."],[3174,"Hosted videos and recordings count towards your storage, metered on the **Plan** tab under **Settings** → **Manage Plan**, with **Buy More**. **Additional Storage (5GB)** is available as an add-on. See storage and upload limits."],[3120,"Hosting is what lets a recorded webinar run. Simulive webinars play the video at times you set, and evergreen webinars play it whenever a registrant's session comes round. Neither works until the video is in the library."],[3170,"Hosting on EasyWebinar is the simpler route for a webinar recording you don't want public. Importing is the quicker route when the video already lives on a platform you control."],[787,"How analytics works with other features"],[4103,"How can attendees pay?"],[2850,"How can I tell if a video is hosted on EasyWebinar or YouTube?"],[2784,"How chat and questions behave in the room is set on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. **Hosts only** makes each attendee's messages private to your team, **No Chat** removes the panel, and Q&A can be public, private or disabled. See Live chat and Questions and answers."],[1405,"How chat behaves also depends on the webinar type. On a live or simulive webinar, everyone in a session is watching the same moment, so the chat works as one shared room. On an evergreen webinar, attendees arrive at different times, so a genuinely shared live chat isn't possible."],[1071,"How chat simulation works with other features"],[1943,"How cloning works with other features"],[1233,"How countdown timers compare"],[1221,"How countdowns work with other EasyWebinar features"],[462,"How course creators use EasyWebinar to sell a course through a webinar, live or automated, from building the webinar to following up and measuring sales."],[92,"How Create with AI works with other features"],[3574,"How custom fields work with other features"],[1518,"How do I add a poll?"],[1787,"How do I add an offer?"],[3589,"How do I ask for marketing consent?"],[1958,"How do I change a webinar's type?"],[4265,"How do I change just one session?"],[4269,"How do I change the price of a paid webinar?"],[3235,"How do I change who the emails come from?"],[963,"How do I check it's working?"],[3716,"How do I check the widget is working?"],[2974,"How do I email the replay to people who missed the session?"],[672,"How do I get a list of everyone who didn't turn up?"],[1965,"How do I get rid of a copy I don't need?"],[2966,"How do I give people the replay?"],[2581,"How do I invite a guest speaker?"],[20,"How do I invite someone to my account?"],[1665,"How do I know how many questions I missed?"],[805,"How do I know if my offer worked?"],[3359,"How do I know if my reminders are working?"],[1243,"How do I know whether the countdown is helping?"],[674,"How do I know which campaign a registrant came from?"],[501,"How do I know which part of my funnel to fix?"],[3977,"How do I let a guest speaker into the room?"],[4267,"How do I let a guest speaker into the room?"],[499,"How do I reach people who didn't show up?"],[1523,"How do I remove an answer option?"],[803,"How do I see how many people didn't turn up?"],[681,"How do I see how many people match my filters?"],[2975,"How do I see how many people watched the replay?"],[3830,"How do I see what the page looks like on a phone?"],[3590,"How do I see which campaign a registrant came from?"],[808,"How do I see which questions I didn't answer?"],[1521,"How do I show a poll during a live webinar?"],[1794,"How do I show the offer during a live webinar?"],[3829,"How do I start from a blank page?"],[2079,"How do I stop a recurring webinar from running on a holiday?"],[1387,"How do I stop attendees chatting to each other?"],[2367,"How do I stop sessions on certain days?"],[112,"How do I tell which webinars were built with AI?"],[233,"How EasyWebinar works, from creating your first webinar to selling, following up and managing your team."],[1206,"How EasyWebinar's countdown timers work on offers and registration pages, why they matter for selling with webinars, and how to set them up honestly."],[72,"How EasyWebinar's Create with AI builds a webinar from a description, writing the script, registration pages, email sequence, polls and offers, and what each step costs in credits."],[3790,"How EasyWebinar's drag-and-drop page builder creates and publishes a webinar's registration page, from picking a template and editing blocks to page-wide settings, AI-written pages and paid registration."],[2552,"How EasyWebinar's green room lets you prepare a live webinar with nothing broadcast, and how backstage holds co-presenters and moderators until you bring them on stage."],[3325,"How EasyWebinar's Webinar Reminders work, how to time them relative to the session, how many to send, and how to tell from Analytics whether they are getting people to attend."],[2358,"How evergreen webinars compare"],[2344,"How evergreen webinars work with other features"],[114,"How hard will the generated offer sell?"],[3356,"How is a reminder's timing set?"],[1658,"How is Q&A different from chat?"],[77,"How it helps"],[466,"How it help