, **Webinar Reminders** and **Webinar Follow-ups** as everyone else, all set on the **Notifications** tab. Reminders are timed relative to the webinar, so they work for recurring and evergreen schedules too."],[791,"Paid registration"],[3221,"Paid registration"],[4251,"Paid registration"],[4190,"Paid registration features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[4130,"Paid registration is for webinars that are the product: workshops, masterclasses, paid trainings and ticketed seminars. People pay to attend, so the seat itself is what you sell."],[4122,"Paid registration makes payment part of signing up. Instead of a free form that registers someone straight away, the registration page shows your price, the **Register Now** button opens a checkout, and the person is registered only once payment succeeds."],[4136,"Paid registration matters most to educators, coaches and consultants whose sessions should earn money rather than cost it. It matters at the planning stage, when a session is designed to be sold rather than given away."],[573,"Paid registration needs the **Paid Webinars** add-on and a connected Stripe account. Registration revenue and course sales from offers inside the session are reported separately under **Revenue by Source**. See Paid webinars."],[96,"Paid webinars"],[1778,"Paid webinars"],[2319,"Paid webinars"],[2954,"Paid webinars"],[4058,"Paid webinars and paid registration"],[1921,"Paid webinars: charging for registration, reported apart from offer sales."],[3320,"Paid webinars: registration happens only after payment, so that is when the confirmation sends."],[3068,"Paid webinars: sell replay access with a Live + Replay bundle."],[4378,"Paid webinars: set a price at creation, since a converted webinar keeps the free form."],[3200,"Paid webinars: the pricing step that comes just before Video Selection."],[3937,"Paid webinars: why the price block appears only when Paid is chosen at creation."],[479,"Paid workshops"],[1230,"Paid workshops and live events"],[4089,"Paid workshops and masterclasses"],[1642,"Pair it with your chat setting"],[2064,"Past dates"],[3751,"Paste the embed code wherever the form should appear."],[1444,"Paste your **Chat widget code**: an `<iframe>` or script snippet, exactly as your chat provider gives it to you."],[4212,"Payments go straight to your Stripe account, and Stripe pays out to your bank on its usual schedule."],[2129,"Payments run through **Stripe**. If no account is connected, a **Payments · Action required** panel offers **Connect with Stripe**. Payouts go directly to your own bank account; EasyWebinar never holds your funds. You can switch back to **Free** any time before creating the webinar."],[643,"People"],[2184,"People"],[2810,"People in the waiting area are moved into the webinar automatically when you go live."],[334,"People is every registrant and attendee across all your webinars in one table, and you can filter it by behaviour and source and export the list. It is a quick way to check who should have received a tag, or to follow up with people outside your CRM rules."],[694,"People is the follow-up list. It turns webinar behaviour into segments you can act on: no-shows to send the replay to, engaged viewers to invite to a call, campaigns that brought attendees rather than just sign-ups."],[4086,"People view"],[2461,"People watching evergreen sessions count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."],[3534,"People watching evergreen sessions count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."],[1026,"People watching evergreen sessions, including just-in-time ones, count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."],[1304,"People who click an offer can be treated differently afterwards:"],[917,"People who reached the checkout for a paid webinar but didn't pay. They aren't registered."],[3323,"People: check who registered and when."],[1629,"People: who answered your polls, next to watch time and offer clicks."],[763,"Phone numbers only appear if your registration form collects them. Add the **Phone** field to the form block."],[719,"Pick a category on the left, refine it on the right, then click **Apply Filter**."],[2260,"Pick a registration template for the page people sign up on, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** to choose one later."],[2426,"Pick a registration template, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** and choose one later. Edit and publish the page in the builder before you send anyone to it. See Registration page builder."],[1587,"Pick any combination of these goals:"],[3654,"Pick the matching CRM field beside each item. The field must already exist in your CRM; after creating one there, click **Refresh**. Integrations are set per webinar."],[331,"Pick the matching CRM field beside each one. **Refresh** pulls in fields you have just created in the CRM."],[1990,"Pick the type for the copy:"],[3409,"Pick whichever channel your audience actually uses. Sending both tends to irritate people."],[4137,"Picture a typical case. A pricing consultant sells tickets to a live, two-hour masterclass for SaaS founders, with seats on sale three weeks ahead. Every founder who buys needs a seat and a join link before the day. Nobody who hasn't paid should get in."],[947,"Plan usage"],[2183,"Plan usage"],[2352,"Plan usage"],[3469,"Plan usage"],[1490,"Polls"],[95,"Polls and offers"],[2692,"Polls and offers"],[2785,"Polls and offers are created on the **CTAs** tab and shown from the room. A row's toggle in the CTAs list keeps an offer ready without showing it. Switch on **Countdown timer** in the offer editor to put a countdown on an offer."],[1597,"Polls and offers share the CTAs tab, the same list controls and the same **Published** switch. A poll asked just before an offer can show you how ready the room is."],[2769,"Polls don't fire on their own in a live session, so plan when each poll goes out. Offers reach the room when you push them from the **Offers** panel. The **Question** panel keeps **Active** and **Answered** apart, so you can see at a glance what's still waiting."],[1025,"Polls, offers and analytics behave as on any webinar. In **People**, filter by **Webinar → Evergreen** to compare your automated funnel with your live sessions. See People."],[3467,"Polls, offers and chat"],[1947,"Polls, offers and emails"],[1749,"Polls: ask the room a question of your own instead of waiting for theirs."],[1920,"Polls: the other kind of CTA, often asked just before the pitch."],[1485,"Polls: the other way to hear from the room, including people who never type."],[432,"Prevent it next time"],[3806,"Preview, save and publish"],[4070,"Pricing on simulive and evergreen webinars"],[1231,"Product and SaaS teams"],[4092,"Professional education"],[1739,"Public if you want people to see what's already been asked. Private if you want control over what the room sees."],[1641,"Public or private?"],[3752,"Publish the page on your site."],[3685,"Put an EasyWebinar registration form on your own website with the Registration Widget embed code, and decide when to use the widget instead of the registration page link."],[1074,"Q&A"],[1701,"Q&A and chat are set side by side on the Engagement tab, and they work best chosen together."],[1684,"Q&A gives attendees a dependable way to ask something and a reasonable expectation that the question will be seen. For the presenter, it turns scattered questions into a list that can be answered in order."],[1669,"Q&A in EasyWebinar is a question queue that runs separately from chat. Attendees submit questions, and you and your moderators work through them in the room's **Question** panel, which splits them into **Active** and **Answered**. You decide on the webinar's **Engagement** tab whether questions are visible to everyone, visible only to hosts and moderators, or switched off. After the session, Analytics shows how many questions were asked and how many you answered."],[1711,"Q&A moderation preferences sit in the room's **Settings**, under **Preferences**, alongside chat moderation and appearance."],[1645,"Q&A on recorded webinars"],[175,"qualifying leads"],[1368,"Questions and answers"],[1631,"Questions and answers (Q&A)"],[1200,"Questions and answers: give real questions a private queue beside the simulated chat."],[1626,"Questions and answers: the attendees' own questions, in a queue."],[1483,"Questions and answers: the question queue you set beside chat on the same tab."],[921,"Questions and answers: the setting behind the **Questions & Answers** panel and its **Not Answered Rate**."],[860,"Read **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** together. A low views-to-clicks rate means the offer itself isn't landing. A low clicks-to-purchases rate means people want the offer but your checkout or price is stopping them."],[3275,"Read the entry. Each one shows its **trigger**, the audience it goes **to**, and its **subject** line, so you can check what it does without opening it."],[1147,"Read through **Preview Simulated Chat**."],[779,"Read your analytics"],[2284,"Recorded webinars also have chat options a live webinar lacks: **Third party** embeds an external chat tool, **No Chat** hides the panel, and the **EW Contact Box** collects attendee questions by email even when chat is off."],[2951,"Recording"],[2877,"Recordings are captured automatically when **Auto Recording** is on in the live room, and appear here after the session. They also show on the **Recordings** tab of the video picker when you set up a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[2921,"Recordings are captured when **Auto Recording** is on in the live room. If the header didn't read **Auto Recording Enabled**, the session wasn't recorded."],[941,"Recurring Schedule"],[2329,"Recurring Schedule"],[3465,"Recurring Schedule"],[2408,"Recurring sessions play at the times you enter, in the webinar's timezone. A session set for 2:00 AM starts at 2:00 AM in that timezone for everyone who picked it."],[340,"Register a test contact and check the tag and fields arrive in your CRM."],[3781,"Register once through it, then look at **Registrants** on the webinar's Overview and find yourself in **People**."],[3753,"Register once yourself through the embedded form."],[289,"Registrants and attendees are different events, so you can treat someone who attended apart from someone who only registered. Without that split, everyone on the list gets the same follow-up, whether they watched to the end or never turned up. That gap is what tracking webinar leads in your CRM is meant to close."],[361,"Registration and selling"],[3341,"Registration confirmation"],[3202,"Registration confirmation emails"],[3441,"Registration confirmation emails: the first email in the sequence, carrying the join link your reminders point back to."],[3684,"Registration embeds"],[3934,"Registration embeds: put the same form on your own site with the Registration Widget."],[3682,"Registration embeds: put this same form on your own site."],[4053,"Registration embeds: when the Registration Widget suits better than a link."],[269,"Registration fields"],[664,"Registration fields"],[4250,"Registration page"],[3789,"Registration page builder"],[4377,"Registration page builder: edit and publish the page the **Registration Page** button opens."],[4054,"Registration page builder: publish the page so the registration link works."],[3318,"Registration page builder: publish the page, or no confirmations go out."],[3784,"Registration page builder: the page your link still needs for email and social."],[3680,"Registration page builder: the rest of the page around the form block, and how to publish it."],[3951,"Registration Page Link"],[1946,"Registration pages and embeds"],[3808,"Registration pages on paid webinars"],[3962,"Registration Widget"],[3267,"Registrations only turn into attendance, and attendance into revenue, if people can find their way into the session. Teams comparing webinar platforms look at whether the confirmation is automatic, whether the sender can be set to their own name, and whether replies reach a real inbox. In EasyWebinar all three are settings on one tab of each webinar."],[574,"Registrations only turn into sales if people attend. The **Notifications** tab handles this:"],[115,"Related"],[367,"Related"],[502,"Related"],[682,"Related"],[812,"Related"],[965,"Related"],[1095,"Related"],[1246,"Related"],[1390,"Related"],[1529,"Related"],[1668,"Related"],[1799,"Related"],[1968,"Related"],[2202,"Related"],[2372,"Related"],[2589,"Related"],[2714,"Related"],[2858,"Related"],[2976,"Related"],[3106,"Related"],[3242,"Related"],[3365,"Related"],[3486,"Related"],[3596,"Related"],[3719,"Related"],[3836,"Related"],[3985,"Related"],[4111,"Related"],[4273,"Related"],[430,"Related problems"],[3217,"Reminder emails"],[766,"Reminder emails: fewer no-shows means a shorter replay list to export."],[3317,"Reminder emails: the emails that follow the confirmation, using the same Email Settings."],[3065,"Reminder emails: the rest of the email sequence around your replay follow-up."],[2458,"Reminder timing on the **Notifications** tab is relative to the webinar, so reminders follow evergreen schedules rather than one fixed date. See Reminder emails and Confirmation emails."],[3345,"Reminders from your own CRM"],[1024,"Reminders on the **Notifications** tab are timed relative to the webinar, not to a fixed clock time, so they work with evergreen schedules. See Reminder emails and Confirmation emails."],[3378,"Reminders sit between two other email groups. The **Registration Confirmation** goes out the moment someone signs up, and **Webinar Follow-ups** go out after the session. Reminders cover the time in between, which is when most registrants forget."],[3401,"Reminders use the webinar's **Email Settings**: the **Sender name** registrants see and the **Reply-to email** where replies go. Set the sender to a name registrants will recognise from their confirmation."],[3031,"Replay emails are set up on the **Notifications** tab, not on the Replay tab. Add a **Webinar Follow-up** after the session, set its audience (everyone who registered, only attendees, or only no-shows) and include the replay link. No-shows are usually the biggest group, and the replay link is what they want. See Reminder emails for the rest of the email sequence."],[2948,"Replay or instant replay?"],[2350,"Replay page"],[2934,"Replay pages"],[2931,"Replay pages: another place a recorded session is watched after the event."],[4055,"Replay pages: how long the Attendee Replay link stays watchable."],[1922,"Replay pages: keep offers selling on the recording with **Webinar Replica**."],[1630,"Replay pages: keep polls on the recording with **Webinar Replica**."],[3443,"Replay pages: the page to send no-shows the reminders didn't reach."],[3555,"Replay pages: the separate page for people who missed a session."],[3201,"Replay pages: where a live session's recording is watched after the event."],[3038,"Replay views are counted separately from live attendance, and someone who did both shows under **Both**. See Webinar analytics and People."],[792,"Replays"],[1371,"Replays"],[1507,"Replays"],[1949,"Replays"],[2181,"Replays"],[4083,"Replays"],[4253,"Replays"],[1223,"Replays and replay deadlines"],[2693,"Replays and the Library"],[3628,"Restyle the submit button if it needs to match your page."],[1125,"Review the attendee list and adjust each simulated attendee."],[3213,"Review the confirmation email"],[6,"Roles"],[2571,"Room design"],[2670,"Run a live webinar"],[1627,"Run a live webinar: the **Polls** panel among the room's other controls."],[1751,"Run a live webinar: the **Question** panel alongside the rest of the room."],[68,"Run a live webinar: the host's path from the device check to ending the session."],[4380,"Run a live webinar: what happens after **Enter Room** and the device check."],[459,"Run a live webinar: what happens after the green room, from going live to ending the session."],[2152,"Run a l