y** to **Daily** or **Weekly**."],[38,"Set a **Password** and **Confirm password**."],[1839,"Set an **Offer Price**, or switch **Free** on."],[3517,"Set any other options you want alongside it: **Just-in-time Registration**, **Recurring Schedule**, **Availability** and **Schedule Preferences**."],[1437,"Set both before you go live rather than in the middle of a session."],[932,"Set it up"],[3211,"Set it up"],[3333,"Set it up"],[3457,"Set it up"],[2560,"Set it up and use it"],[3395,"Set its timing before the webinar."],[1014,"Set the **Interval** to 2 minutes, the shortest option."],[841,"Set the date range and click **Apply**. The range applies to every number on the page, so if a webinar looks emptier than you expected, widen it first."],[562,"Set the evergreen schedule, and turn on just-in-time."],[1018,"Set the interval back to your chosen value once you're done."],[1045,"Set the interval to 2 minutes, register on your own page, and watch for the session on the **Live** tab of the Sessions panel."],[578,"Set the sender name to something your students recognise, and the reply-to address to one someone reads."],[2406,"Set the time sessions should start."],[3392,"Set the timing as time before the webinar, in hours, minutes and seconds."],[1475,"Set them beforehand. These controls are part of the webinar's setup rather than the live room."],[2943,"Set up a replay page"],[2158,"Set up a simulive webinar in EasyWebinar that plays a pre-recorded video at the dates and times you schedule, with a shared chat you can answer in while it plays."],[1063,"Set up AI Simulation"],[1215,"Set up an offer countdown"],[994,"Set up any other options you want alongside it: **On Demand**, **Recurring Schedule**, **Availability** and **Schedule Preferences**."],[1356,"Set up chat"],[1066,"Set up Manual Simulation"],[1640,"Set up Q&A"],[2669,"Set up Q&A: set up the question queue a moderator will work through."],[1841,"Set up the **Button**: size, icon, text and **Button URL**."],[3567,"Set up the registration form"],[1218,"Set up the registration-page countdown"],[4069,"Set your price"],[935,"Settings"],[3460,"Settings"],[2569,"Share links"],[3700,"Share links"],[3812,"Share links"],[2953,"Sharing"],[3940,"Sharing links"],[2815,"Sharing links: the co-presenter and moderator links that bring people backstage."],[3935,"Sharing links: the link that only works once this page is published."],[3785,"Sharing links: the Registration Page Link and One-Click Registration Link that sit beside the widget."],[4376,"Sharing links: who gets each link behind **Share**, and which to keep private."],[3958,"Shorten the links"],[1003,"Shorter intervals mean less waiting. The interval is the longest a new registrant waits for the next just-in-time session, so 2 minutes keeps the wait to a couple of minutes and 60 minutes can mean close to an hour."],[3485,"Should every evergreen webinar have On Demand on?"],[1967,"Should I clone before testing changes on a running webinar?"],[2587,"Should I set up EasyCast in the green room?"],[3361,"Should I test a text or WhatsApp reminder first?"],[3715,"Should I use the widget or the registration page link?"],[1659,"Should questions be public or private?"],[1770,"Show an offer during the webinar"],[2083,"Sign in to EasyWebinar. **Any team member can create a webinar**; you don't need to be the account owner."],[301,"Sign in to that service and allow access."],[1171,"Simulated attendees can show in the attendee list too, with **Show attendee list on event page**. The webinar-wide **Show Attendees** setting on the **Settings** tab controls whether attendees see the list at all."],[555,"Simulated attendees make the room look populated. They shouldn't claim results or endorse your course."],[1166,"Simulated chat is there to stop an automated room looking empty. It isn't a place for social proof that didn't happen."],[2507,"Simulive"],[2023,"Simulive and evergreen copies play a video from the Library. Recordings of webinars you've already run appear under **Recordings** automatically when auto recording was on, ready to pick on the copy's **Content** tab. See The Library."],[1510,"Simulive and evergreen webinars"],[2838,"Simulive and evergreen webinars"],[3086,"Simulive and evergreen webinars"],[4153,"Simulive and evergreen webinars have the same **Free** or **Paid** choice. On those types, the pricing step comes after the schedule and before **Continue to Video Selection**, where you pick the recording the sessions will play."],[3107,"Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording, so before you can run one you need a video in your library. EasyWebinar gives you two ways to get it there. **Local import** uploads the file and EasyWebinar hosts it for you, so you don't need a separate video host. **Import from URL** plays a video that already lives on **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or at a direct **MP4** link. The route you pick decides whether the video uses your storage and whether you need to tell EasyWebinar how long it runs."],[2885,"Simulive and evergreen webinars play a video from your library:"],[2276,"Simulive is for a presentation you give again and again, or a session scheduled at an hour you'd rather not be awake for. You record the talk once, and EasyWebinar broadcasts it at the times you choose, like a scheduled programme."],[1076,"Simulive webinars"],[1363,"Simulive: answer while the recording plays"],[888,"Single-webinar reporting, from each platform's public help docs:"],[101,"Small businesses and solo operators"],[951,"Small businesses and solo operators"],[1079,"Small businesses and solo operators"],[2357,"Small businesses and solo operators"],[3093,"Small businesses and solo operators"],[3822,"Small businesses and solo operators"],[3677,"SMS and WhatsApp (both Beta) go to the phone number from the registration form. Add the **Phone** field first."],[3655,"SMS and WhatsApp notifications, both in Beta, are set on the **Notifications** tab and go to the phone number from your registration form. Without the **Phone** field on the form, there's nobody to message. Reminder emails cover the email side."],[3219,"SMS and WhatsApp welcome messages (Beta)"],[572,"Some course creators charge for the webinar itself: a paid masterclass, a workshop, or a paid preview of the course. Choose **Paid** when you create the webinar, set the price in US dollars, and attendees pay through Stripe as they register. Turn on the **Live + Replay bundle** to sell the recording too."],[1573,"Some practical habits:"],[2543,"Someone registers on your registration page, paying first if the webinar is paid."],[976,"Someone who arrives at your page at 2:07 can be watching by 2:15, instead of waiting until tomorrow. The recording is the same one your other evergreen sessions play; only the start time changes."],[235,"Start here"],[1415,"Stay on **Chat**, the first of the four sections (**Chat**, **Q&A**, **AI Moderation** and **Chat Simulation**)."],[3387,"Stay on the **Emails** channel and find the **Webinar Reminders** group."],[1930,"Step 1: Open the clone dialog"],[2060,"Step 1: Open the create dialog"],[2161,"Step 1: Open the create dialog"],[4233,"Step 1: Read the four stats"],[2324,"Step 1: Start a new webinar"],[4234,"Step 2: Check or change the schedule"],[1931,"Step 2: Choose the type of the copy"],[2325,"Step 2: Name it and choose Evergreen"],[2162,"Step 2: Name it and choose Simulive"],[2061,"Step 2: Name your webinar and choose its type"],[2326,"Step 3: Build the schedule"],[4236,"Step 3: Manage individual sessions"],[1932,"Step 3: Name the copy"],[2163,"Step 3: Set the schedule"],[2062,"Step 3: Set your schedule"],[2068,"Step 4: Choose free or paid"],[2164,"Step 4: Choose free or paid"],[2332,"Step 4: Choose free or paid"],[1933,"Step 4: Choose what to copy"],[4237,"Step 4: Set free or paid registration"],[4238,"Step 5: Add presenters and moderators"],[2070,"Step 5: Choose a registration template"],[2165,"Step 5: Choose the recording"],[2333,"Step 5: Choose the video"],[1934,"Step 5: Create the copy"],[2334,"Step 6: Choose a template"],[1935,"Step 6: Finish a copy that changed type"],[2168,"Step 6: Pick a registration template"],[4240,"Step 6: Share the webinar"],[4241,"Step 7: Enter the room"],[438,"Still stuck?"],[2839,"Storage and your plan"],[3088,"Storage and your plan"],[484,"Stream to your existing audience"],[273,"Streaming"],[4210,"Stripe. Connect your Stripe account on the pricing step or from **Integrations → Payment**."],[641,"Style the live room: backgrounds, overlays and layout so the room matches your course brand."],[2947,"Style the page in the builder"],[261,"Supported integrations"],[2268,"Swapping the video leaves your schedule, pages and registrations as they were. That makes it safe to replace a presentation with an improved cut while sessions are already booked."],[1860,"Switch off the toggle on the offer's row in the **CTAs** list, or"],[1858,"Switch on **Countdown timer** to put a countdown on the offer card. It's a single toggle, set on each offer separately. Use it when the offer really does close or change at a set time, and say in the sub headline what ends."],[1270,"Switch on **Countdown timer**."],[3053,"Switch on **Enable replay page** and send the **Replay Page Link**. It's also in the **Share** dialog as **Attendee Replay link**."],[3004,"Switch on **Enable replay page**. The page then reads *Replay page is live, anyone with the link can watch*."],[991,"Switch on **Just-in-time Registration**."],[3515,"Switch on **On Demand**."],[2402,"Switch on as many of the three viewing options as you like. Each one you enable shows on the registration page as a choice."],[862,"Switch to **People** to see who registered and who attended. For a full list across all your webinars, with columns such as watch percentage, offer clicked and lead score, plus filters and export, use People in the sidebar."],[863,"Switch to **Revenue**."],[426,"Symptom"],[736,"Tag the links in your ads, emails and posts as you normally would."],[3634,"Tag the links you share as you normally would, in ads, emails and posts."],[1263,"Take a typical case. A business coach runs an evergreen webinar that plays twice a day and ends on an offer for a twelve-week coaching programme. Anyone who enrols before their session ends gets a bonus strategy call. The coach is rarely watching, and every session has a new audience."],[521,"Take a typical example. A course creator opens enrolment with a live webinar in launch week, presenting to an email list and answering questions in the chat. The launch closes, but new subscribers keep arriving. The creator wants that same pitch to enrol them without presenting it every week."],[3960,"Team & Moderators"],[365,"Team and account"],[1,"Team members and roles"],[2568,"Team members and roles"],[458,"Team members and roles: who joins as a co-host or moderator, and how they get in."],[4239,"Team members are a different thing"],[9,"Team members, presenters and moderators"],[4056,"Team members: logins for colleagues, as opposed to join links for guests."],[4381,"Team members: when to give someone a login instead of a join link."],[2783,"Teams choosing a live webinar platform want to know that a live session will look composed, that they can sell during it, and that they'll have a recording afterwards. The live room covers all three in one place, and the recording feeds the replay and the evergreen version of the same webinar."],[1552,"Teams choosing a webinar platform want engagement tools that are quick to set up and that work the same way whether the webinar is live or recorded. Polls in EasyWebinar are built once on the CTAs tab and apply to live, simulive and evergreen webinars alike, and AI can draft the first set."],[3127,"Teams moving to automated webinars want to know whether they need a video host as well as a webinar platform. In EasyWebinar they don't: uploads are hosted directly, and importing from YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia is an option rather than a requirement. Buyers also check file formats and size limits before recording, and how storage is counted when a library grows."],[3740,"Teams that already run websites and blogs want webinar registration to sit inside the content that brings in traffic. Buyers check whether the platform lets them embed a form, whether they can adjust its look, and whether it's a simple copy-and-paste."],[2901,"Teams that plan to run recorded webinars want to know where the video lives, whether they need a separate video host, and how storage is counted. In EasyWebinar the answers sit in one screen: EasyWebinar can host the file itself, imported links use no storage, and live recordings arrive in the same place ready to reuse."],[1690,"Teams that run demos, trainings and sales webinars want to answer questions without losing control of the room. Being able to keep chat sociable while routing questions into a private queue, and then checking afterwards how many were left unanswered, is the practical version of that control."],[2282,"Teams that run the same webinar on a cycle, such as a weekly product walkthrough, a monthly onboarding session or a standing sales presentation, want consistency without giving up a live audience. Simulive gives them a polished recording, set session times and a chat they can staff."],[2021,"Teams that run webinars as a programme reuse what works. Being able to duplicate a proven webinar, or move it from a live format to an automated one, without rebuilding it, is what makes that practical."],[4006,"Teams that run webinars with guest speakers, moderators and existing customer lists need to give each person the right access quickly and safely. Buyers check whether presenters can join without their own seat on the account, whether existing contacts can register without friction, and whether the replay can be shared as easily as the webinar."],[2606,"Teams that run webinars with more than one speaker (panels, interviews, product walkthroughs with a moderator) need guests to join without disrupting the session. A green room with a backstage area is what makes a multi-presenter webinar look composed, and buyers comparing tools for live webinars look at how guests join and whether they can wait off stage."],[3512,"Teams using evergreen webinars for education and onboarding want people to get the content when they ask for it. On Demand gives registrants immediate access from the same registration page, recording and webinar setup."],[938,"Test a just-in-time session"],[3339,"Text and WhatsApp reminders (Beta)"],[3573,"Text reminders (Beta)"],[3957,"Thank You Page Link"],[693,"That changes what you can do after a session. Instead of knowing that a large share of registrants missed the webinar, you can see who they are, narrow the list to one webinar, and export it for a replay email. Instead of knowing that some people clicked your offer, you can find the ones who watched most of the session, clicked, and still haven't bought."],[2457,"The **AI Moderator** answers attendee questions from documents you upload and keeps the chat civil. It is in Beta. It's aimed at large webinars and automated ones running without you."],[1023,"The **AI Moderator**, in Beta, answers attendee questions from documents you upload and keeps the chat civil. On an automated webinar running at 3am, it can answer a question that would otherwise wait for someone on your team."],[740,"The **Analytics** tab on a single webinar shows the funnel and offer numbers; People shows the individuals across all webinars. Use Analytics to find where a webinar is leaking, then People to find who is in that gap. See Webinar analytics."],[3766,"The **Clone Webinar** dialog lists **Embed widgets** under **Webinar assets**, alongside registration pages, the webinar schedule and replay settings. Leave it ticked to copy the widget into the new webinar."],[1812,"The **CTAs** tab holds two kinds of call to action. A poll asks your audience something. An offer asks them to do something: buy, book, enrol, download."],[324,"The **Custom fields** tab sends webinar details into your CRM's own fields: \"Choose which of your CRM's custom fields should receive each piece of webinar data.\""],[2643,"The **Design** panel sets the background, a frame overlay and the stage layout. Layout matters most when several presenters are on stage or someone is sharing a screen."],[1450,"The **EW Contact Box** is a built-in question and contact form for attendees, and it works even when chat is off. **No Chat** plus a pinned contact box suits a presentation you don't want interrupted but still want questions from."],[2880,"The **Files** tab is also where the AI Moderator's documents live. The AI Moderator is in **Beta**: it answers attendee questions from documents you give it, reading **PDF, DOCX or PPTX** files up to **25MB** each, and it retrains every time you add a source."],[824,"The **Overview** view is built around a funnel. People arrive at the registration page, some register, some of those attend live or watch the replay, and some never show up. Below the funnel sit the numbers for what happened during the session: chat, questions, and how your offers performed."],[825,"The **People** view lists who registered and who attended. The **Revenue** view breaks down what the webinar earned, separating paid registrations from offers sold in the room."],[333,"The **Phone Number** field only has something to send if your registration form collected it. Select the form block in the page builder and add the **Phone** field; custom registration fields covers the other fields you can add."],[743,"The **Phone** column fills only if your form collects it. Add the **Phone** field, or your own fields, on the registration form block. See Custom fields."],[2289,"The **Plan** tab, under **Settings** → **Manage Plan**, counts people watching simulive and evergreen sessions on its **Automated attendees** meter, separately from **Live attendees**."],[2248,"The **Recordings** filter is where earlier webinars show up. If you ran a session live with recording on, its recording can become the content of this simulive webinar."],[3295,"The **Registered** metric in a webinar's Analytics counts unique sign-ups, which is the number of people your confirmation should have reached. The **People** view lists each registrant with a **Registered on** column. See Webinar analytics and People."],[3243,"The **Registration Confirmation** email is the first message a new registrant gets from your webinar. EasyWebinar sends it immediately after someone registers, and it carries their attendee join link, which makes it the email that actually gets people into the session. It sits on the webinar's **Notifications** tab, and the **Email Settings** button on the same screen decides whose name your emails show, where replies go, and whether an admin address receives a copy of each registration."],[3905,"The **Registration Page Link** in the Share dialog is the published page's address, and the **Registration Page** button on the webinar header opens the live page."],[3720,"The **Registration Widget** lets people register for your webinar without leaving your own website. On the webinar's **Content** tab you copy its **Embed Code** and paste it into your page wherever the form should appear: a landing page, a blog post, a sidebar. The same snippet is in the **Share** dialog, and **View & Customize** lets you change how the widget looks before you copy it."],[3904,"The **Registration Widget** on the Content tab gives you embed code to put the form on your own page instead of sending people to the EasyWebinar page."],[3531,"The **Replay** tab controls a separate page for people who missed a session, with availability options of **Always Available**, **Expire after days** or **Specific date**, and an **Experience** of **Webinar Replica** or **Custom Build**. Those settings belong to the replay page, not to On Demand."],[2988,"The **Replay** tab holds everything about the page people use to catch up on a past session. It has five parts:"],[1886,"The **Revenue** view splits earnings under **Revenue by Source**, separating paid registrations from offers sold in the room. Offer sales show under **Paid Offer**."],[4311,"The **Sessions** panel lists every sitting of the webinar under its own tab:"],[2641,"The **Share** dialog on the webinar holds seven links, including the presenter and moderator ones above. **Shorten URL's** gives you shorter versions. See Sharing links."],[337,"The **Social media** category on the Integrations tab is separate from CRMs. To broadcast a webinar to YouTube or LinkedIn while it runs, use EasyCast, under **Integrations** in the sidebar."],[4023,"The **Team & Moderators** panel on the Overview is the other way to bring people into a webinar: **Add presenter** adds someone who appears on camera and presents, and **Invite** sends an invitation to join the webinar team. A join link suits a guest on one session; adding someone to your account team suits people who work in EasyWebinar regularly."],[3289,"The **Thank you Page** is one of the five pages on the **Content** tab and appears straight after registering. On a paid webinar, it shows the attendee's **Webinar join link** with a **Join Room** button, and the session **Date** with **Add to Calendar** buttons for Google, Outlook and Apple. The page and the email cover the same moment from two sides: one in the browser, one in the inbox."],[2267,"The **Webinar Video** panel on the **Content** tab shows the selected recording and its length. **Preview** plays it back, and **Change Video** swaps it for another."],[163,"The AI drafts a full sequence:"],[1747,"The AI Moderator is in Beta. In **Suggest Answer** mode it drafts answers for you to approve; in **Answer directly** mode it answers without approval."],[1724,"The AI Moderator, in Beta, has a **Q&A Moderation** screen. With **Suggest Answer** it drafts an answer for you to approve before attendees see it; with **Answer directly** it answers without host approval. It doesn't replace a human moderator on a live webinar."],[2907,"The AI Moderator's knowledge base documents live on the **Files** tab. Because the moderator retrains with each new source, give it a moment after an upload before you test it."],[3896,"The AI then writes your registration page, thank-you page and waiting area, using the script as source material: headline, what you'll learn, instructor bio and the rest. The pages open in an editor with **Edit**, **Preview**, **SEO** and **Scripts** tabs, and a desktop and mobile view. Treat the output as a strong first draft; afterwards, pages open in the normal builder."],[162,"The AI writes your registration page, thank-you page and waiting area, using the script as source material: headline, what attendees will learn, an instructor bio and the rest. The pages open in an editor with **Edit**, **Preview**, **SEO** and **Scripts** tabs and a desktop and mobile view. Treat them as a strong first draft. Click **Continue**."],[823,"The Analytics tab is the per-webinar report. It answers two questions: how many people got through each stage, from landing on the registration page to watching, and where the others stopped."],[4159,"The attendee lands on a Stripe checkout page showing your business name and the webinar as the item. They can pay by card, or by Apple Pay or Link where available. Their email is carried over from the registration form, so they don't type it twice."],[1073,"The attendee list"],[3801,"The builder controls"],[2096,"The builder opens on **Step 1 of 4: Build**."],[2735,"The button stays greyed out until the room can see a camera and a microphone. If it can't open your camera, you'll see **\"Not able to access selected media device\"**. Allow camera access in your browser and close any other app that's using the camera. Camera not detected walks through the fixes."],[2616,"The button stays greyed out until the room can see a camera and a microphone. If you see **\"Not able to access selected media device\"**, see Camera not detected."],[1072,"The Chat setting"],[3641,"The checkbox is a form option. What it asks for, and how you use the data afterwards, is yours to decide."],[3261,"The confirmation does two jobs at once. It tells the registrant that signing up worked, and it hands them the join link they will need later. EasyWebinar's own guidance calls it the one email you shouldn't turn off, because every other step of getting someone into the room depends on them having that link."],[3259,"The confirmation is the only one of the five tied to the moment of sign-up. Reminders count down to the session, follow-ups react to what happened in it, and the transaction email answers a purchase. The confirmation answers a registration."],[3288,"The confirmation starts the email sequence and **Webinar Reminders** carry it to the session. Reminders share the same **Email Settings**, so the sender a registrant learns from the confirmation is the one they see again before the webinar. See Reminder emails."],[3410,"The confirmation starts the sequence and carries the join link; reminders bring the registrant back to it. Both are on the same tab and share the same sender settings."],[3803,"The countdown block"],[1300,"The countdown is part of an offer, so everything about the offer still applies: its price, its button and where that button goes. Point the button at the checkout for exactly the offer the timer describes."],[838,"The counts are built to avoid double counting. **Visitors** counts unique IPs on the landing page. **Total Attended** counts each person once and files them under **Live only**, **Replay only** or **Both**. How other platforms report on a single webinar is covered in How webinar analytics compares, below."],[1067,"The CSV format"],[1887,"The date range at the top of Analytics applies to everything on the page, so widen it if an offer looks emptier than expected."],[3526,"The deciding question is whether the webinar is valued for its content or for the occasion."],[3525,"The default *Watch instant replay* works, but the word \"replay\" can suggest a recording of something people missed. If your page sells the webinar as fresh content, wording that says what happens next, such as starting the training now, can read more naturally. Whatever you choose, keep it short enough to fit a button."],[2138,"The default form collects **Full name** and **Email**, both required. Use **Add Custom Field** to collect more on the form."],[2451,"The demo is the same every week, so the presenter is not what makes each session work. Once it is recorded, sessions can repeat by themselves. The wait can then shrink to minutes for anyone who registers between Tuesdays."],[449,"The device check shows your camera preview and microphone, and **Continue to Green Room** becomes clickable. Nothing in the green room is broadcast; the header reads **Not Live** until you click **Go Live**."],[1214,"The EasyWebinar approach to countdown timers"],[2343,"The EasyWebinar approach to evergreen webinars"],[4067,"The EasyWebinar approach to paid webinars"],[469,"The EasyWebinar approach to selling courses"],[778,"The EasyWebinar approach to webinar analytics"],[3203,"The email EasyWebinar sends the moment someone registers, carrying their join link, and the Email Settings that control the sender name, reply-to address and admin copies."],[3291,"The emails step of **Create with AI** drafts a full email sequence, beginning with a welcome email on registration and followed by reminders and follow-ups. After the build, the emails sit on the **Notifications** tab like any others. See Create a webinar with AI."],[564,"The enrolment offer is a card with a headline and a button, shown in the room when you're ready."],[264,"The events you can trigger on"],[187,"The flow ends on the new webinar's **Overview**. From here it works exactly like a webinar built by hand."],[3804,"The form block"],[3903,"The form block is where you collect more than name and email."],[3607,"The form block's settings add four things on top of that:"],[3656,"The form is one block on the registration page. Everything else on the page, from the template to the countdown and page-wide settings, is covered in Registration page builder."],[3881,"The form starts with **Full name** and **Email**, both required. Selecting the form block lets you add a **Phone** field and your own custom fields, turn on **GDPR Compliance** and **UTM Params**, and restyle the submit button. Each of these is covered under Custom fields, consent and UTM capture below."],[4350,"The four stats are a summary of what the **Analytics** tab shows in detail. A brand-new webinar shows zeros on both until registrations start."],[997,"The full creation walkthrough, including pricing, video selection and templates, is in Create an evergreen webinar."],[202,"The generated sequence lives on the **Notifications** tab with every other email, where you can change subjects, content and timing. See Confirmation emails and Reminder emails."],[2551,"The green room and backstage"],[2590,"The green room is the private state of the EasyWebinar live room before a broadcast starts. You and your team can test cameras, microphones and screen sharing and arrange the stage, while the header reads **Not Live** and nothing reaches attendees. Backstage is the waiting area inside the room: co-presenters and moderators arrive there, off stage, and appear to the audience only when you move them on."],[2737,"The green room is the room as it will look, with nothing broadcast. Check your framing, test **Share**, and get your co-hosts in place."],[2600,"The green room separates getting ready from being seen. Presenting live involves a handful of things that can go wrong in the first minute: a muted microphone, the wrong camera, a screen share showing the wrong window, a guest who can't hear. The green room gives you time to find those problems while nobody is watching."],[2758,"The header now shows **LIVE** with a timer of how long you've been broadcasting, the recording badge changes to **Recording**, and **Go Live** becomes **End Session**. If you're streaming with EasyCast, a platform icon appears for each destination. Click it to open the stream on that platform and see what viewers there are seeing."],[1852,"The headline and sub headline do the selling, so give each a job:"],[338,"The integration shows under **Connected apps** as **Ready to use**."],[2182,"The Library"],[2817,"The Library"],[3085,"The Library"],[1945,"The Library and recordings"],[2895,"The Library is the shared store behind your webinars. It is where simulive and evergreen webinars get their content, where finished live sessions end up, and where your storage allowance is spent. Keeping it in one place means a video added once can be used by any webinar that needs it."],[2053,"The Library: where the recording of a live original waits to be picked."],[3064,"The Library: where the recordings your replay pages play are kept."],[640,"The Library's recordings: where your live session's recording lands before you clone it as Evergreen."],[3999,"The links fall into three kinds. **Audience links** (registration, one-click registration, attendee join, attendee replay) are meant for the people watching. **Team links** (co-presenter and moderator) let someone into the room in a role, so they're private. The **Thank You Page Link** is where registrants arrive on their own, so you rarely need it."],[13,"The live room"],[2836,"The live room"],[3961,"The live room"],[2776,"The live room is where a live webinar actually happens. Everything you set up beforehand (the registration page, reminders, polls, offers) leads to this hour. The room gives you a private place to prepare, a clear moment to start, the tools to engage and sell while you present, and a definite end."],[443,"The live room needs a working **camera and microphone** before it lets you into the green room. The button stays greyed out until the room can see both. You can turn them off once you are in, but you can't enter without them."],[2903,"The live room's header shows **Auto Recording Enabled** when recording is on, and the badge changes to **Recording** once you're live. Recording can be changed under **Settings → Recording Settings**, and recorded sessions land in **Library → Recordings**. See Run a live webinar."],[444,"The message appears when the room can't open the camera or microphone you selected."],[1139,"The mix of attendees decides whether the chat reads as real. A room full of enthusiastic experts posting constantly looks staged. A few beginners asking basic questions, one sceptic, a couple of quiet observers on low engagement and some mid-level regulars looks like an audience."],[3500,"The names overlap, so the two are easy to mix up."],[56,"The new member appears in the Team list with their role and joined date, and the seat count on the Settings overview goes up by one."],[2511,"The objects you work with"],[1256,"The offer countdown lives inside the **offer** itself, so it travels wherever that offer is shown. The registration-page countdown is a **block** on the page, so you style and position it like any other part of the page."],[1284,"The offer stays ready but does not appear until you switch it on."],[1280,"The offer's **Title** is internal. Attendees never see it, so name it in a way that helps your team, for example \"Course enrolment, launch week\"."],[11,"The Overview tab"],[4188,"The Overview tab has a **Convert to paid** button for free webinars. If you convert an existing free webinar to paid, its registration page keeps the free form, so people can still register without paying. Create a new webinar and choose **Paid** on the pricing step instead."],[4222,"The Overview tab has a **Convert to paid** button, but the registration page of a converted webinar keeps the free form. Create a new webinar and choose **Paid** on the pricing step instead."],[4341,"The Overview tab is the home screen for one webinar. It answers the questions you ask most often (is anyone registering, when does it run, what does it cost, who is presenting, which link do I send) without opening any of the other eight tabs."],[2054,"The Overview tab: checking the copy's schedule and its empty registrant count."],[2667,"The Overview tab: where **Enter Room** opens the green room for a session."],[3787,"The Overview tab: where **Registrants** confirms your test registration."],[3939,"The Overview tab: where the **Registration Page** button opens the live page."],[4052,"The Overview tab: where the **Share** button sits, next to **Registration Page**."],[1050,"The Overview tab: where the Live tab shows a just-in-time session on air."],[919,"The Overview tab's live stats: four of these numbers at a glance, updating while the webinar runs."],[3575,"The page builder"],[3922,"The page needs to be published. Open it in the builder and click **Publish**. Saving alone isn't enough."],[2000,"The panel at the bottom of the dialog repeats the new webinar's name and type before you commit. Read it once: it's the last chance to catch a wrong type, which can't be changed afterwards."],[237,"The parts of EasyWebinar"],[270,"The People view"],[1508,"The People view"],[1777,"The People view"],[3571,"The People view"],[3702,"The People view"],[644,"The People view in EasyWebinar lists every registrant and attendee across all your webinars, with watch percentage, offer clicks and lead score, and lets you filter by behaviour or campaign and export the result."],[70,"The People view: every registrant and attendee across your webinars, with filters and export."],[1580,"The poll stays on the webinar, ready to switch on, and nothing is deleted."],[1572,"The polls that get answered ask about the attendee, not about what they remember. A question about their situation, their plans or their biggest problem takes a second to answer and needs no right answer. A knowledge test feels like an exam, and people skip it."],[3902,"The price block is added only when **Paid** is chosen at creation. A free webinar converted to paid afterwards keeps the free form, so choose **Paid** at creation if you want to charge."],[4012,"The public link to your registration page, and the one you promote in ads, emails and posts. It only works once the registration page has been published in the page builder; saving alone isn't enough."],[523,"The recording of the live session already holds the pitch that worked. What needs to change is who presses play: each new registrant, at a time that suits them, rather than the creator."],[3606,"The registration form is a block on the registration page, like the countdown or a heading. Its settings decide what a person is asked when they sign up. Out of the box it asks for a name and an email address, both required."],[3699,"The registration page"],[4073,"The registration page"],[3856,"The registration page decides how much of your promotion turns into an audience. Buyers check how quickly they can get a credible page live, whether it matches their brand, whether they can see which campaign drove each signup, and whether the page lives on their own domain."],[4348,"The registration page is built on the **Content** tab and opened from the **Registration Page** button here. The **Registrants** stat counts people who complete its form."],[3762,"The registration page is still where your webinar's full pitch lives: the design, the countdown, the copy. Build and publish it in the page builder even if most registrations come through the widget, because the link and the page are what you'll use in email and on social."],[539,"The registration page is the link you promote, so it carries most of your signups. It opens in a drag-and-drop builder with your date, time and timezone already in place."],[3837,"The registration page is the page people see before they sign up, and the link you promote. EasyWebinar builds it in a drag-and-drop page builder that already carries your webinar's date, time and timezone, with a countdown and a name-and-email form in place. You choose a template, edit blocks on a canvas, check the mobile layout, and click **Publish** to make the page public. The same builder edits the webinar's other four pages."],[3847,"The registration page matters most because it carries your signups. It's built from **blocks**, such as the date and countdown block and the form block, plus whatever else the template includes. You select a block on the canvas to change it, add new blocks underneath, and set page-wide options such as fonts, background and tracking from the top bar."],[4042,"The registration page needs to be published. Open it in the page builder and click **Publish**."],[4156,"The registration page shows the price above the form."],[3849,"The registration page turns interest into a registrant. It tells a visitor what the webinar is and when it runs, asks for the details you need, then hands them on to the thank-you page."],[481,"The replay"],[3032,"The replay link also appears in the webinar's **Share** dialog as **Attendee Replay link**, alongside the registration and attendee join links meant for your audience. See Sharing links."],[583,"The replay link is public while the replay page is on, so treat it as something anyone can share."],[3466,"The replay page"],[1873,"The replay page has two looks, set on the **Replay** tab:"],[2994,"The replay page is also the fifth of the five webinar pages on the **Content** tab, after the registration page, thank-you page, waiting area and webinar page. The Replay tab decides how the page behaves; the Content tab is where you can style it in the page builder."],[2459,"The replay page on the **Replay** tab is for people who missed a session that has already happened. It is separate from On Demand. See Replay pages."],[764,"The result count is shown below the table."],[128,"The result is a normal EasyWebinar webinar. It has the same nine tabs and the same settings as one built by hand. The only visible difference is the **AI** badge on its card in **My Webinars**."],[2803,"The room needs to see a working camera and microphone before it lets you in. See Camera not detected."],[455,"The same fixes apply on their computer. Co-hosts and moderators who get in land backstage, not on stage, so your audience doesn't see or hear them until you bring them on. A guest co-host or moderator joins with the Co-presenter Join Link or the Moderator Join Link from the Share dialog."],[2395,"The schedule step is where an evergreen webinar differs from every other type. It offers three ways for people to watch, plus controls for when the schedule runs."],[2412,"The schedule step shows a message saying attendees will see times in their local time based on the selected timezone. On an evergreen webinar that applies to just-in-time sessions only. Daily and weekly sessions run at the times you set, in the webinar's timezone."],[2235,"The schedule step shows a message saying attendees will see times in their local time. For simulive sessions that isn't how they run: they play at the times you set, in the webinar's timezone. Only just-in-time sessions on evergreen webinars follow each attendee's local time."],[2228,"The schedule step works the same way it does for a live webinar."],[194,"The script and pages are the expensive steps, which is another reason to get the prompt right before you generate. Each step shows your balance before you commit, and you can switch off any output chip to skip that part."],[537,"The script downloads as a PDF so you can present from it. A full build uses about 23 credits."],[160,"The script is organised into named sections, such as the hook and welcome and the problem framing, each with its own timing and speaker notes. Read it before you continue. Fixing the script now is much easier than fixing the pages and emails built from it. Click **Continue to landing pages**."],[3950,"The seven links"],[3941,"The seven links in an EasyWebinar webinar's Share dialog, from the registration page link you promote to the one-click registration, attendee, co-presenter, moderator and replay links, and who each one is for."],[3763,"The Share dialog groups every way to share a webinar: **Share Links**, **Registration Widget** and **Share on social media**."],[51,"The Share dialog holds a Co-presenter Join Link for a presenter and a **Moderator Join Link for Live room** for someone who handles chat and questions. Treat both as private. Anyone holding one can join your room in that role."],[3994,"The Share dialog is the single place to copy any link a webinar produces. Click **Share** on the webinar's header and the dialog opens with three groups:"],[4025,"The Share dialog's **Registration Widget** holds the same embed snippet as the **Content** tab. Use it to put the form on your own site instead of sharing a link."],[2275,"The short version: simulive is a broadcast of a recording on a timetable. It sits between live, where you present every time, and evergreen, where the schedule runs continuously and each person picks their own time. For the evergreen setup, see Create an evergreen webinar."],[2871,"The small badge in the corner of each card shows where the video is hosted:"],[4297,"The stat cards across the top tell you, at a glance, whether people are signing up and turning up."],[3218,"The thank-you page"],[4221,"The thank-you page shows their personal join link, a **Join Room** button, the session date and **Add to Calendar** buttons for Google, Outlook and Apple. They also get your confirmation email."],[2505,"The three webinar types"],[2090,"The three webinar types use the same pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics. Only the delivery differs."],[2504,"The three webinar types, what every webinar is made of, and how registration, the room, follow-up and analytics fit together."],[1985,"The top of the dialog sets out what 