 Rate** is a useful check after a busy session: it tells you how many questions you left behind."],[3658,"The webinar's **Analytics** tab counts visitors and registrations. The People view's **Source & UTM** filter shows which campaign produced attendees, not just registrations."],[3412,"The webinar's **Analytics** tab shows the funnel from **Visitors** to **Registered**, **Live Attended**, **Total Attended** and **Missed**. Two gaps tell you different things:"],[1872,"The webinar's **Settings** tab has an **End of Session** URL, which is empty by default. Point it at your offer or booking page so attendees aren't left sitting on a finished webinar. **Expired Session** does the same for anyone arriving at a link that has expired."],[3734,"The widget is for keeping people on your site. If a visitor is already reading your page, the shortest path to a registration is a form right there, not a link to somewhere new."],[184,"Then describe what you're selling and where the button should send people, and pick an offer category: online course, coaching programme, membership, digital product or service package. Click **Generate Offers**."],[1868,"Then describe what you're selling and where the button should send people. Pick a category (online course, coaching programme, membership, digital product or service package) and click **Generate Offers**. You get complete offers, each with a title, headline, sub-headline, button text and link. Tick the offers you want to keep, then click **Save and continue**. The offers step costs 1 credit."],[2028,"There is no Delete for webinars. If you don't need a copy, choose **Archive** from its card menu and it moves to the **Archived** tab."],[4371,"There's a **Convert to paid** button, but the registration page of a converted webinar keeps the free form. Create a new webinar and choose **Paid** on the pricing step instead."],[1614,"There's no practical limit. Add as many as the session needs."],[4302,"These are headline numbers. For the 