 happens"],[259,"Why it matters"],[927,"Why just-in-time matters"],[1351,"Why live chat matters"],[1758,"Why offers matter"],[3452,"Why On Demand matters"],[4062,"Why paid webinars matter"],[1494,"Why polls matter"],[1635,"Why Q&A matters"],[3688,"Why registration embeds matter"],[3328,"Why reminders matter"],[2938,"Why replay pages matter"],[2685,"Why running the room well matters"],[3944,"Why sharing links matter"],[2172,"Why simulive matters"],[3206,"Why the confirmation email matters"],[2555,"Why the green room matters"],[2829,"Why the Library matters"],[425,"Why the live room can't open your camera or microphone, and how to get into the green room."],[4244,"Why the Overview tab matters"],[647,"Why the People view matters"],[3793,"Why the registration page matters"],[3074,"Why video hosting matters"],[773,"Why webinar analytics matters"],[1791,"Why won't my offer save?"],[1084,"Why would I simulate chat?"],[3697,"Widget or link: which to use"],[435,"Will attendees see me while I fix my camera?"],[3834,"Will EasyWebinar translate my page?"],[282,"Will it sync people who registered but didn't attend?"],[498,"Will it work with my email tool?"],[3979,"Will my co-presenter appear on screen as soon as they join?"],[2969,"Will my offers and polls show on the replay?"],[1795,"Will my offers show on the replay?"],[1241,"Will my offers, and their countdowns, show on the replay?"],[1524,"Will my polls appear on the replay?"],[1092,"Will the AI chat be the same in every session?"],[1170,"With **Easywebinar Chat** selected, a recorded webinar's Chat screen offers **Simulated Chat**, which plays back a pre-written chat during the webinar, and **Simulated Attendees**, which shows a simulated attendee list in the room. The script, attendee count and names are set on the Chat Simulation tab. Choosing **Third party** replaces the built-in chat, so simulation stops applying."],[3118,"With **Import from URL**, the answer is somewhere else. You give EasyWebinar the platform, a link and the video's length, and the webinar plays the video from that platform. Nothing is stored on EasyWebinar, so no storage is used, but the webinar now depends on the video staying where it is."],[3117,"With **Local import**, the answer is EasyWebinar. You upload the file, EasyWebinar stores and serves it in the same way a dedicated video host would, and nothing else is needed to play it in a webinar. The upload uses part of your storage allowance, shown at the top of the Library."],[1301,"With **Webinar Replica**, the replay page shows the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the session, so your offers keep selling after the event. The replay itself can also have a deadline: **Expire after days** closes it a set number of days after the session, and **Specific date** closes it at a time you choose. A replay deadline and an offer deadline are separate settings; keep them consistent so attendees aren't told two different end times."],[472,"With AI"],[1261,"With no countdown, an offer's end point is easy to miss or forget. People who meant to buy are left unsure whether it is still open. Many wait, and in webinar selling, waiting often means not buying. A registration page with no visible start time gives visitors little reason to sign up today."],[3528,"With On Demand off, registrants still have just-in-time or recurring sessions if you've enabled them."],[3619,"With only name and email, you know how many people registered but very little else. You can't text anyone, and you can't tell which ad, email or post sent them. UTM capture is the option people most often miss: without it, the registration count goes up and the reason why is lost."],[987,"With only recurring times, a visitor who arrives just after a session has started faces a wait until the next slot, which may be hours or a day away. The gap between interest and watching is where people disappear: they close the tab meaning to return, and many don't."],[4178,"With the replay page set to **Webinar Replica**, the recording shows the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the session. Replay availability is set on the **Replay** tab, and **After the replay ends** under Redirects can send viewers to your next offer."],[699,"Without a behaviour-level list, every registrant gets the same follow-up. The person who watched to the end and clicked your offer receives the same \"sorry we missed you\" email as someone who never turned up, and the people closest to buying are treated like everyone else."],[3855,"Without a builder tied to the webinar, you'd design a landing page in one tool, wire its form into the webinar platform, and update the date by hand every time the schedule moved. Each of those is a place for a broken form or a wrong time to slip through, and the page you promote is the one place a mistake costs registrations directly."],[3001,"Without a replay page, the session is over for everyone who wasn't there at the time. No-shows receive a follow-up with nothing to watch, a viewer who reaches the end of the recording has nowhere to go, and an offer made live has no second audience. EasyWebinar's guidance is to leave live recording on for this reason: the replay is usually watched by more people than the live session."],[1689,"Without a separate queue, questions compete with every other message in chat. The presenter scrolls back looking for them, misses some, and answers others twice. Attendees whose questions were missed leave unsure, and on a selling webinar an unanswered objection often decides the sale."],[2900,"Without a shared library, every recorded webinar would need its video uploaded again, and recordings of live sessions would have to be downloaded and re-added before you could reuse them. It would also be harder to tell which videos sit on YouTube or another platform, which is how a webinar ends up playing a video someone has since deleted elsewhere."],[4346,"Without a single summary screen, the basics of a webinar get scattered. You check the schedule in one place, pricing in another and the presenter list somewhere else, and it's easy to promote a webinar with the wrong date or forget to add a co-presenter until they message you asking for a link."],[2782,"Without a staging area, presenters test their microphones in front of the audience, and a co-host's first words are an apology about echo. Without a confirmation step, a webinar can start before the offers exist. Without automatic recording, the replay you planned to send to no-shows may not exist at all."],[2605,"Without a staging area, the first few minutes of a webinar become the rehearsal. Attendees who arrived on time watch presenters ask each other whether they can be heard, and the recording that will later become your replay page starts with the same fumbling. Guest speakers who join late interrupt the session in progress."],[519,"Without a webinar in the middle, people go straight from an email or an ad to a sales page. The page has to answer every doubt on its own, with no chance to teach or take questions. Visitors who aren't ready yet tend to leave."],[3739,"Without an embed, every visitor on your own site has to follow a link to the EasyWebinar page to register. Each extra click and page load is a chance for someone to get distracted and leave, and the context that persuaded them (the article they were reading, the page they landed on) is left behind."],[2447,"Without an evergreen schedule, a recording reaches people only on the dates it is shown. Anyone who finds the page between showings has to wait, and many lose interest before the next one comes round."],[1826,"Without an offer card, the call to action is whatever the presenter says and whatever link gets pasted into chat. Late arrivals miss it, chat scrolls it away, and on a recorded webinar nobody is there to repeat it. After the session there is no record of who was interested enough to click, so everyone gets the same follow-up."],[3126,"Without built-in hosting, every recorded webinar would depend on another platform: an account to manage, privacy settings to get right, and a video that anyone with access to that channel could remove. A YouTube video is still a YouTube video, discoverable unless you've unlisted it. Hosting on EasyWebinar keeps the recording and the webinar in one place."],[1412,"Without chat, attendees have no way to speak during the session, and the presenter has no way to tell whether the message is landing. Questions go unasked or arrive by email after the moment has passed. For a selling webinar, that is where doubts that could have been answered in a sentence turn into \"not now\"."],[2020,"Without cloning, changing a webinar's format would mean building the second version by hand: recreating the registration page, rewriting the emails, re-entering polls and offers, and reconnecting integrations. Each one is a chance to introduce a difference you didn't intend."],[135,"Without it, the setup work is spread across several blank pages: a script document, a page builder, five or six emails and an offer. That's often where webinars stall, especially for a first session, and the pieces written on different days tend not to match each other."],[3511,"Without On Demand, every registrant has to wait for a session, even if only a few minutes with just-in-time. For content people want to consume as soon as they find it, any wait is a chance for them to leave and not return."],[4135,"Without paid registration, the registration page signs up anyone for nothing. A workshop worth paying for becomes a free session. Its value then has to be won back later, through an offer that only some attendees buy."],[832,"Without per-stage numbers, a disappointing webinar is just disappointing. You can't tell whether few people saw the page, the page didn't convert, the reminders failed or the offer fell flat. So you end up changing everything at once. It's easy to rewrite a talk that was fine, when the real problem was that people never turned up."],[1551,"Without polls, the main signal from the audience is chat, which only reflects the people who choose to type. The presenter guesses at what the room wants, attention drifts during long sections, and after the session there is little record of who took part beyond attendance."],[3384,"Without reminders, attendance depends on people remembering a session they signed up for days or weeks earlier, and finding their confirmation email at the right moment. Analytics makes the cost visible: a large **Missed** count, people who registered and never showed up, with a registration page that was doing its job. EasyWebinar's own reading of a low registered-to-attended rate is that it's a notification problem, not a content one."],[4005,"Without role-specific links, the only way to bring a guest speaker into the room is to give them access to your account. And without a one-click link, every contact you invite from your own list has to retype details you already hold, which is a reason for some of them not to bother."],[2281,"Without simulive, a recurring presentation means presenting live each time, at whatever hour the audience needs. The alternative, a fully automated webinar where people watch at different times, loses the shared conversation, because attendees arriving at different points have nothing in common to talk about."],[3461,"Wording the button"],[445,"Work through these in order and check the device preview after each one."],[83,"Write a prompt that works"],[1068,"Write a script that reads like a real room"],[1501,"Write polls people will answer"],[767,"Write polls people will answer: the **Polls** column only tells you something if people answer them."],[1765,"Write the card"],[3396,"Write the subject and content."],[1144,"Write your script in the four columns and save the file as **CSV (UTF-8)**."],[221,"Yes, all of it. Pages open in the page builder, emails on the **Notifications** tab, and polls and offers on the **CTAs** tab."],[3783,"Yes, f